Disclaimer
------------------------------------------------------------------------

   The Reference Frame is defined to be EME2000 [1].
   
   The Epoch is defined to be Jan 1 2000 12:00 (2451545.0D0).

   NOTE: These keywords break the 32 character limit for SPICE
   kernel pool variable names. EME2000 and epoch J2000 are the
   defaults so it's not necessary to explicitly put them in.

        BODY920065803_CONSTANTS_REF_FRAME   = (  1           )
        BODY920065803_CONSTANTS_JED_EPOCH   = (  2451545.0D0 )

        BODY120065803_CONSTANTS_REF_FRAME   = (  1           )
        BODY120065803_CONSTANTS_JED_EPOCH   = (  2451545.0D0 ) 
 
 
Applicability of Data
--------------------------------------

   The rotation parameters for Dimorphos are only valid prior to the
   DART impact time of 2022 SEP 26 23:14:24.184 UTC. 
   
   Most users should use the switch frame DIMORPHOS_FIXED, defined in
   didymos_system_007.tf and later versions of the frame kernel.
   DIMORPHOS_FIXED is valid for all times before and after the DART
   impact.


Orientation Constants
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Didymos
--------------------------------------

   Didymos has a volume-equivalent diameter of 710.3 m, using
   the best-fit dimensions from [4].

   The spin pole is taken to be longitude 310.0 degrees, latitude -80.6
   degrees in the ECLIPJ2000 frame.

   The spin period is taken to be 2.2600 +/- 0.0001 hours.

   The Prime Meridian for Didymos is arbitrarily set to 0 at the epoch.
   
   \begindata

        BODY920065803_RADII             = ( 0.39167, 0.39167, 0.29195 )
        BODY920065803_POLE_RA           = (  69.326861266078069, 0, 0)
        BODY920065803_POLE_DEC          = ( -72.724550395829496, 0, 0)
        BODY920065803_PM                = (  0.0, 3823.008849557522, 0.0  )
        BODY920065803_PGR_POSITIVE_LON  = 'EAST'

   \begintext


Dimorphos
--------------------------------------

   Dimorphos has a volume-equivalent diameter of 145.6 m, using
   the best-fit dimensions from [4].

   This PCK corresponds to the Dimorphos orbit solution 542. It is
   designed to keep the body-fixed X-axis of Dimorphos oriented
   towards the Didymos primary center of mass.  It is only valid prior
   to the DART impact time of 2022 SEP 26 23:14:24.184 UTC.  

   The frame IAU_DIMORPHOS is constructed from these parameters.  It
   will be the same frame before and after impact.  Most users will
   probably want to use the switch frame DIMORPHOS_FIXED, defined in
   the frame kernel didymos_system_007.tf.  DIMORPHOS_FIXED is
   equivalent to IAU_DIMORPHOS prior to impact and is a dynamic frame
   after impact, where the X axis points from Dimorphos to Didymos and
   the Z axis is parallel to the IAU_DIDYMOS Z axis.
   
   \begindata
   
        BODY120065803_RADII            = ( 0.09078, 0.06932, 0.06131 )
        BODY120065803_POLE_RA          = (  69.326861266078069, 0, 0)
        BODY120065803_POLE_DEC         = ( -72.724550395829496, 0, 0)
        BODY120065803_PM               = (  73.070565080143595,  
                                           724.724388306834840, 
                                             1.0270736140e-06)

        BODY120065803_PGR_POSITIVE_LON = 'EAST'

   \begintext
        

GM values 
------------------------------------------------------------------------

   The GM of the system is taken from [4].

   The individual GM values are derived from the system GM, scaled by the 
   relative volumes calculated from the dimensions given above
   and assuming the same density for both bodies.

   System GM = 3.48961209875640268354e-08 km^3/s^2
   Didymos volume (va) = 0.1876 km^3
   Dimorphos volume (vb) = 0.001616 km^3

   GM for Didymos   = [ va / (va + vb) ] * 3.48961209875640268354e-08
                    = 3.45980739686124e-08
                  
   GM for Dimorphos = [ vb / (va + vb) ] * 3.48961209875640268354e-08
                    = 2.9804701895163013e-10

   Units below are km^3/s^2.
   
   \begindata


      BODY20065803_GM   = 34.8961209875640268354E-9
      BODY120065803_GM  = 0.29804701895163013E-9
      BODY920065803_GM  = 34.5980739686124E-9

   \begintext


End of PCK file.
